        "id": 11245,
        "name": "BrettTurner",
        "username": "BrettTurner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ac8455/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-06T13:23:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>OK, summarizing what I read in other threads,</p><p>1.&nbsp; He is countermix limited to 12 structures.</p><p>2.&nbsp; The structures can stack.</p><p>3.&nbsp; They are triggered the moment anyone moves or his pushed into the hex, plus once in each character's To Be Continued phase if the character is standing in a hazard.</p><p>4.&nbsp; They do not trigger upon creation.</p><p>5.&nbsp; All ice patches go away if Absolute Zero switches active cards so that the card which allows creation of Impaling Strucutres is no longer in his three-card hand.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>(1) Is this all correct; (2) is there any other way Impaling Structures go away?&nbsp; Can they be attacked with powers?&nbsp; Do they disappear if stacked with lava?&nbsp; Can Absolute Zero remove an Ice Stucture at will without swapping the card out?&nbsp; (We were playing yes on this last point but I now think we did it wrong.) (3) if multiple structures are stacked in one hex, does EACH structure get a separate attack?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks,</p><p>--Brett Turner</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:30.512Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
